  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 is our best RNA encoder (0.520 acc) vs pca_n2000 (0.485), and image alone (resnet50) is very weak (0.208). The key unresolved question is whether the multiprofile setting with aggregation improves upon the singleprofile baseline. This experiment (config_005: scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) is a clean, single-variable extension of config_004 (same encoder, same modality; only profile setting changes from single to multi with avgpool aggregation). It isolates the effect of multiprofile+aggregation while holding the best-known encoder fixed. Choosing avgpool over transformer keeps the test conservative and interpretable: if avgpool already helps, multiprofile is validated; if it doesn't, we can then test transformer (config_006) to rule out aggregation-method effects. This is the highest-information next step because the multiprofile decision gates many downstream configurations and will determine whether to invest further in aggregation design or pivot to encoder/fusion questions."
